<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="ai_buildout_and_bust::capital_flow_rate" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Escalating kinetic activity raises regional geopolitical risk premiums and investor uncertainty, prompting reallocation away from riskier tech and infrastructure bets and reducing net capital flows into AI projects tied to the region or exposed supply chains.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="ai_buildout_and_bust::regulatory_constraint_in" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising conflict prompts governments to impose export controls, sanctions, foreign‑ownership limits and heightened national‑security reviews that directly increase regulatory restrictions on AI buildout and operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in Iran-Gulf conflict intensity forces the US and key allies to reallocate munitions, surveillance assets, and logistical lift to the Middle East, slowing or reducing the volume and cadence of weapons and ammunition deliveries destined for Ukraine.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="russia_ukraine_war::multinational_coop" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A significant uptick in Iran-Gulf conflict intensity produces competing operational priorities and threat perceptions among allies (some focused on regional deterrence, others on Europe), creating friction and reducing alignment and coordination on sanctions, timing of aid, and joint actions regarding Russia.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::conflict_intensity" target="tech_trade_and_chip_riva::export_control_tightness" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rise in kinetic attacks and military incidents prompts immediate national security responses (sanctions, licensing reviews, targeted denial lists) that expand and tighten outbound technology controls to deny dual‑use goods and tech to perceived adversaries.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_trade_and_chip_riva</data>
</edge>
