<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price_level" target="ai_buildout_and_bust::corporate_ai_investment_" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained higher oil prices increase energy and input costs and compress corporate margins, causing firms to defer or scale back discretionary capital expenditures such as AI infrastructure, tooling and R&amp;D.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price_level" target="russia_ukraine_war::domestic_polit_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher oil prices driven by Iran-Gulf tensions raise household energy and transport costs across NATO states, increasing inflationary pressure and voter dissatisfaction and thereby intensifying domestic political constraints on leaders' foreign-policy flexibility.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price_level" target="tech_trade_and_chip_riva::resource_nationalism" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sustained higher oil prices increase rents for resource exporters, giving governments fiscal room and political incentive to tighten export rules, prioritize domestic processing, or assert control over upstream and related inputs.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_trade_and_chip_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price_level" target="us_political_realignment::regulatory_direction" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in global oil prices creates political pressure to boost domestic energy output, leading executives and legislators to fast-track deregulatory measures (e.g., expedited permitting, relaxed constraints) that shift net regulatory direction toward deregulatory policies.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
