  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">An uptick in strikes against energy and transport infrastructure increases local grid unreliability and insurance/financing costs, which directly depresses ground‑up starts and slows planned data‑center construction in affected regions.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_freq" target="iran_gulf_conflict::oil_price_level" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in kinetic strikes in Ukraine elevates global risk premia for energy supply and logistics (insurance, transit routes), prompting immediate upward pressure on benchmark crude prices.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::kinetic_strike_freq" target="us_political_realignment::policy_clarity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Sharp upticks in strike frequency create rapid operational changes that compel faster, sometimes contradictory public statements and ad hoc requirements for assistance, reducing the clarity and credibility of policymakers' commitments in the short term.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
