<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::domestic_polit_pressure" target="ai_buildout_and_bust::corporate_ai_investment_" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising domestic political pressure tied to the war prompts governments and firms to tighten scrutiny of foreign partnerships and to favour politically safe, short‑term expenditures, causing firms to delay or scale back corporate capital expenditures on AI R&amp;D and infrastructure.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::domestic_polit_pressure" target="iran_gulf_conflict::negotiation_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising domestic political pressure in donor governments to prioritize resources and political capital for the Ukraine effort reduces diplomatic bandwidth and willingness to invest in Gulf mediation, lowering the momentum and resourcing of formal talks.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::domestic_polit_pressure" target="tech_trade_and_chip_riva::export_control_tightness" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising domestic political pressure on allied governments accelerates legislative and administrative moves to restrict exports of dual‑use tech and chips to countries seen as supporting the aggressor, tightening controls independent of multilateral action.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_trade_and_chip_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::domestic_polit_pressure" target="us_political_realignment::exec_leg_alignment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising domestic political pressure (from polarized constituencies, interest groups, and donors reacting to the war) pushes the executive and differing congressional blocs toward contradictory demands and postures, increasing executive–legislative friction over foreign policy and funding decisions.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
