<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::multinational_coop" target="ai_buildout_and_bust::regulatory_constraint_in" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Greater coordinated action among allies in response to the war produces harmonized export controls, sanctions and joint screening regimes that directly raise the intensity and scope of regulatory restrictions on AI-related trade, investment and operations.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::multinational_coop" target="tech_trade_and_chip_riva::export_control_tightness" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.85</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher alignment among external states produces coordinated sanction packages and harmonized control lists, prompting governments to broaden and tighten outbound technology export rules in a synchronized fashion.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_trade_and_chip_riva</data>
</edge>
<edge source="russia_ukraine_war::multinational_coop" target="us_political_realignment::regulatory_direction" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.8</data>
  <data key="d36">Higher allied coordination on sanctions and export controls generates political and technical pressure on U.S. agencies and Congress to adopt tighter regulatory measures (sanctions lists, export controls, tariffs, CFIUS-like restrictions) to harmonize policy with partners.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">russia_ukraine_war</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
