<edge source="ai_buildout_and_bust::capital_flow_rate" target="russia_ukraine_war::domestic_polit_pressure" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A decline in capital flows into AI (a buildout bust) produces layoffs, revenue shortfalls and fiscal strain in electorally important tech and supplier sectors, increasing domestic political pressure on governments to reprioritize spending and constrain foreign assistance; conversely rising capital flows relieve that pressure.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_buildout_and_bust::capital_flow_rate" target="tech_trade_and_chip_riva::crossborder_capital_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A surge in AI-directed capital (VC, PE, sovereign allocations) attracts foreign LPs, syndication and cross‑border M&amp;A, directly raising the volume of cross‑jurisdictional tech finance.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
  <data key="d39">tech_trade_and_chip_riva</data>
</edge>
