<edge source="ai_buildout_and_bust::corporate_ai_investment_" target="iran_gulf_conflict::conflict_intensity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased corporate AI investment by defense contractors accelerates production and export of AI-enabled ISR and targeting systems to regional militaries and proxies, raising the tempo, precision and lethality of kinetic operations in the Gulf.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
  <data key="d39">iran_gulf_conflict</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_buildout_and_bust::corporate_ai_investment_" target="russia_ukraine_war::military_aid_flow" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased corporate AI investment accelerates development and commercial-scale production of AI-enabled ISR, loitering munitions and counter‑UAS systems that allied suppliers can procure and donate more rapidly, raising the volume and cadence of external military assistance.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_war</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_buildout_and_bust::corporate_ai_investment_" target="us_political_realignment::regulatory_direction" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A sharp increase in corporate AI investment finances concentrated lobbying, trade‑association pressure and industry‑backed rulemaking petitions that push legislators and regulators to adopt deregulatory language and delay restrictive rule rollouts, shifting net regulatory direction toward deregulatory outcomes.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_buildout_and_bust::corporate_ai_investment_" target="us_political_realignment::legislative_control_bala" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising corporate AI investment generates increased political contributions and targeted local spending by firms and PACs that improve electoral prospects for pro‑industry candidates, incrementally increasing the dominant coalition's legislative margin in competitive districts.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_buildout_and_bust</data>
  <data key="d39">us_political_realignment</data>
</edge>
